# DAY 13 — Complete System Integration & Testing

## Objective

Integrate and test the complete EV Dashboard and ADAS Warning System developed during the internship.

## Modules Integrated

The following modules are combined and tested:

* EV Control System
* ADAS Warning System
* Fault Management
* Vehicle State Machine (FSM)
* UART Command Shell
* Python EV Dashboard
* Ultrasonic Sensor Interface
* Motor Control using PWM

## System Testing

### 1. Normal Driving

The system operates in the `STATE_DRIVING` state during normal driving conditions.

The EV controller calculates:

* Vehicle speed
* Motor torque
* Battery SOC
* Motor temperature
* Driving mode
* Regenerative braking

### 2. Forward Collision Warning

The front ultrasonic sensor continuously monitors the distance to an obstacle.

Warning conditions:

* Distance < 50 cm
* TTC < 3 seconds

Critical conditions:

* Distance < 20 cm
* TTC < 1.5 seconds

The ADAS module generates the appropriate collision warning level.

### 3. Blind Spot Detection

Left and right ultrasonic sensors are used for blind-spot monitoring.

Blind-spot warning is activated when:

* Object distance < 30 cm
* Vehicle speed > 20 km/h

### 4. Fault Detection

The fault-management module monitors critical system conditions.

Implemented faults:

* `FAULT_OT` — Motor over-temperature
* `FAULT_SOC` — Critically low battery SOC
* `FAULT_COL` — Critical collision

When a critical fault occurs, the vehicle state changes to:

```text
STATE_FAULT
```

Motor torque is disabled and the fault indication is activated.

### 5. Fault Recovery

The UART command:

```text
fault clear
```

clears the active faults and returns the EV to:

```text
STATE_PARKED
```

The vehicle values are reset to a safe condition.

### 6. UART Testing

The UART shell provides commands for system testing and monitoring.

Important commands include:

```text
help
status
mode eco
mode normal
mode sport
speed set <kmh>
soc set <pct>
temp set <degC>
obstacle <cm>
obstacle clear
fault inject motor
fault inject soc
fault inject col
fault clear
alarm test
reset
```

These commands allow different EV and ADAS conditions to be simulated and tested.

### 7. Python Dashboard

The Python dashboard receives telemetry through UART and displays:

* Vehicle speed
* Battery SOC
* Motor torque
* Motor temperature
* Estimated range
* Accelerator and brake values
* Front, left and right obstacle distances
* Time-to-collision (TTC)
* Collision warning
* Blind-spot status
* Alarm level
* Fault status
* Drive mode

The dashboard also supports a demo mode without hardware.

## Result

The EV control, ADAS, fault-management, FSM, UART and Python dashboard modules were integrated into a single system.

The system can detect safety conditions, generate warnings, enter a fault state when required, and provide real-time telemetry through the Python dashboard.

## Key Learning

Day 13 focused on **system-level integration and testing**, connecting individual embedded modules into a complete EV ADAS prototype.
